  "claim": "A breed the of spaniel was developed in New London, Wisconsin. That breed was derived before the Estonian Hound.",
  "evidencia": "Page: English Water Spaniel. Sentence: The English Water Spaniel is a breed of dog that has been extinct since the first part of the 20th century, with the last specimen seen in the 1930s.\nPage: Estonian Hound. Sentence: It was bred in 1947 when the Soviet Union's national economy ministry decided that every country in the Union must have its own dog breed.\nPage: American Water Spaniel. Sentence: The breed was saved by Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer, who set up the breed club and standard, and whose work led to recognition for the breed by the United Kennel Club, and later, the American Kennel Club.\nPage: New London, Wisconsin. Sentence: The American Water Spaniel was developed as a registered breed by F. J. Pfeifer of New London.",
