        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bee3ef5c-2093-5b1f-8800-17ee5bb89202",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: English Water Spaniel, Estonian Hound, American Water Spaniel\n- People: Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer, F. J. Pfeifer\n- Organizations: Soviet Union national economy ministry, United Kennel Club, American Kennel Club\n- Places: New London, Wisconsin\n\nFacts:\n- The English Water Spaniel is an extinct dog breed, and the last specimen was seen in the 1930s after the breed disappeared in the first part of the 20th century.\n- In 1947, the Estonian Hound was bred after the Soviet Union's national economy ministry decided that every country in the Union must have its own dog breed.\n- Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer saved the American Water Spaniel by establishing the breed club and breed standard.\n- Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer's work led to recognition of the American Water Spaniel by the United Kennel Club and later by the American Kennel Club.\n- F. J. Pfeifer of New London, Wisconsin, developed the American Water Spaniel as a registered breed.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
